 "description": "<p>UPV4&nbsp;at 72°30&nbsp;N -&nbsp;59°00&nbsp;W&nbsp;is a standard hydrographic station&nbsp;on the Upernavik section and&nbsp;part of the Greenland Institute of Natural Resources monitoring program. The purpose of the marine monitoring program is to register specific&nbsp;physical properties&nbsp;of the sea water column,&nbsp;such as temperature and&nbsp;salinity,&nbsp;at the same geographical location&nbsp;once every year, and compare these repeated registrations&nbsp;with&nbsp;previous years' recordings. Hydrographic measurements are&nbsp;typical carried out with a so-called \"CTD\" instrument (Conductivity, Temperature, and Depth). The hydrographic station is&nbsp;monitored one time each year&nbsp;in June/July.</p>",
